        "section_max_width": 1400,
        "media_first_mobile": true,
        "subheading": "How Honey Cloudz Helps",
        "heading": "Confidence Starts With Comfort™",
        "text": "<p><strong>Feeling comfortable in your body again shouldn't feel out of reach</strong>.<br/><br/>You've already been through enough between the appointments, the procedures, the recovery period, and all the emotional ups and downs that come with navigating a body that may look and feel different than it once did.<br/><br/>Yet for many women, the options available afterward feel like an afterthought.<br/><br/>Hot and heavy silicone forms that leave your shoulders and back aching by the end of the day. Breast forms that trap heat, build up odor, and feel uncomfortable against your skin.<br/> <br/>Limited solutions for lumpectomy, explant, and breast balancing needs. Products designed to serve a medical purpose—but not necessarily help you feel comfortable, confident, and like yourself again.<br/><br/><strong>You deserve </strong><em><strong>better.</strong></em><br/><br/>Our lightweight breast forms and balancing inserts are designed to restore volume, shape, and symmetry while prioritizing the comfort that so many traditional options overlook. <br/><br/>Lightweight enough for everyday wear. Breathable enough to stay comfortable throughout the day. Designed to stay secure enough where you put them.<br/><br/>But what truly makes us different isn't just our products—<em><strong>it's how we create them.</strong></em><br/><br/>We listen.<br/><br/>Every design starts with real women, real feedback, and real experiences. <strong>We obsess over comfort, test on real bodies, and continuously improve our products based on the stories, challenges, and needs our community shares with us every day.</strong><br/><br/>Because post-op solutions shouldn't feel clinical. They should feel personal.<br/><br/>Join over 67,000 women who have discovered cloud-soft comfort designed to help them feel supported, balanced, and more like themselves again.<br/><br/></p>",
        "button_label": "",
