    "custom_reviews_masonry_wBRfLt": {
      "type": "custom-reviews-masonry",
      "blocks": {
        "review_HYxyHx": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "rating": 5,
            "headline": "I feel so more confident and pretty in my clothes",
            "text": "<p>“I’m almost one year post double mastectomy and the original silicone breast forms I purchased were exciting to get being I was flat, but soon learned how heavy and hot they can be and still healing that was a lot of weight on my chest..so I found I don’t wear them. As I creep up on my one year I’m ready to start wearing cute clothes again and if you know you know being flat can not look as flattering as one would hope.. so here I am trying Honey Cloudz and needless to say<strong> I’m in love they fit perfectly in my Soma bra’s and I feel so more confident and pretty in my clothes. </strong>I purchased both teardrop and circle in a small and love both I’m 5’3, 140lbs… I think I’ll try a medium next just to have options on size.. the price was amazing too I spent $250 out of pocket for my original breast forms… so far I’ve worn my honey cloudz more than my original set purchased I hardly notice I’ve got them on their that light weight! Thank you for thinking of us mastectomy girls 🫶🏻”<br/><br/></p>",
            "author": "Erin O.",
            "show_verified": true
          }
        },
        "review_mDW4nJ": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "rating": 5,
            "headline": "Very happy with the quality and the confidence it gave me",
            "text": "<p>\"Just last week I was finally able to try the oval breast forms after my mastectomy.I must say, I was very happy to wear the forms. <strong>Felt normal light weight and very comfortable.</strong> I am so glad I choose these brand. Very happy with the quality and the confidence it gave me. Thank you so much.\"</p>",
            "author": "Nutan P.",
            "show_verified": true
          }
        },
        "review_BfdAyb": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "rating": 5,
            "headline": "Honey Cloudz are lightweight, you barely feel them!",
            "text": "<p>“This is a product I have been waiting for, having a double mastectomy, I have been using bra inserts and cotton fill as typical prosthesis' are too heavy. Honey Cloudz are lightweight, you barely feel them! <strong>They are comfortable, form to the chest wall, and I have extra skin and am not flat.</strong> They are breathable, ok to wear in the summer heat. I purchased the XL and had wide large breasts, these fit perfectly into any bra with an opening. I will be ordering more!”</p>",
            "author": "Melissa M.",
            "show_verified": true
          }
        },
        "review_9WpA4H": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "rating": 5,
            "headline": "I CANCELED my reconstruction consult with a plastic surgeon!!",
            "text": "<p>“I had a bilateral mastectomy in 2023 due to breast cancer. I was comfortable being flat for years but now I'm starting to look more like my old self but something was missing. I’ve tried wearing expensive, heavy silicone inserts but they are so uncomfortable after a while. I ordered these thinking I'd give it a try. I CANCELED my reconstruction consult with a plastic surgeon!!<strong> These are so natural, light and comfortable!! I will definitely be ordering another set! </strong>10/10 hands down recommend.”</p>",
            "author": "Kayla",
            "show_verified": true
          }
        },
        "review_F6hV3j": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "rating": 5,
            "headline": "Really happy with them and the confidence boost.",
            "text": "<p>“I am post double mastectomy and purchased 2 of these ovals 'extra forms. I am not sure if I will get reconstruction. I liked the idea of lightweight forms and the big plus that they stay in place without being the heavy all silicone kind. <strong>These are wonderful! They look very natural in everything I've tried them in.</strong> Really happy with them and the confidence boost.”</p>",
            "author": "Pam Y.",
            "show_verified": true
          }
        },
        "review_QgWGet": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "rating": 5,
            "headline": "I look and feel like myself again!",
            "text": "<p>“This being my 2nd go around with mastectomy surgery, I can give an honest, experienced comparison of mastectomy forms! Five years ago I was fitted with a hot, heavy, sweaty, uncomfortable, silicone form and was unable to wear it for five months after surgery! Fast forward to Feb. 2026, my second mastectomy. Three weeks after surgery I was comfortably wearing Honey Cloudz teardrop forms. <strong>Natural, light weight, cool and comfortable! I am so grateful.</strong> To top it all off, the company is personable, communicative and so easy to order from! I just ordered my second pair to keep a fresh set ready to wear! Thank you, Angela, Anna & Danielle! You made a difficult time a lot easier! I look and feel like myself again! 😁”</p>",
            "author": "Jane S.",
            "show_verified": true
          }
        },
        "review_Hy9P4f": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "rating": 5,
            "headline": "It's freedom from being uncomfortable all the time. HOORAY!!!",
            "text": "<p>“I am quite amazed with my new lightweight boobs :) Double mastectomy 13 years ago, no reconstruction. For 13 years I have weathered the heavy, rubbery, sweat-inducing breast forms from the cancer center at the hospital. The bra was always tugging and lopsided because the breast forms were so heavy and sticky. Tried the Honey Cloudz teardrop shape. I was driving yesterday and<strong> almost forgot I had a bra and boobs on! They are comfortable, LIGHT WEIGHT and not sweat inducing.</strong> I am completely happy with my HoneyClouds. It's freedom from being uncomfortable all the time. HOORAY!!!”<br/><br/></p>",
            "author": "Liz N.",
            "show_verified": true
          }
        },
        "review_cjKCEX": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "rating": 5,
            "headline": "Thanks for helping me heal again",
            "text": "<p>“I had to get my implant removed after 20 years due to a complication. I was not mentally prepared to face being one sided. I tried a couple of forms but they were itchy and poked me. I put in a Honey Cloudz teardrop breast form and<strong> immediately felt better. Really better. You can barely feel it. It fits perfectly and it's incredibly comfortable. </strong>I cannot thank you enough for creating a product I never knew I would need. I am so lucky to have found you and ordered several more. Thanks again for helping me heal again.”</p>",
            "author": "Nancy F.",
            "show_verified": true
          }
        },
        "review_tLCPd7": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "rating": 5,
            "headline": "Your product is the only one that I have found that works for meYour product is the only one that I have found that works for me",
            "text": "<p>“I have been looking for a bra insert that works for me for the last six years following my mastectomy. I have tried many different products, including a prosthesis through my health insurance, and all of them have been too large and/or too heavy for my petite size. Your product is the only one that I have found that works for me. <strong>I am so grateful to have found you, and now feel the search is over. Please do not stop making these. </strong>Thank you, thank you, thank you!!”</p>",
            "author": "Sarah N.",
            "show_verified": true
          }
        },
        "review_R8yC8q": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "rating": 5,
            "headline": "I plan on telling my surgeons about your products",
            "text": "<p>“After my bilateral mastectomy, my doctors referred me to a mastectomy specialty shoppe. Because Medicare would pay, I was fitted with a lot of such uncomfortable 'garbage'! It was a total waste of my time and I could tell it was all about taking advantage of a breast cancer patient. I am ecstatic over my purchase from Honey Cloudz &<strong> I LOVE my breast forms. I just ease them into my bras & they look super natural.</strong> I plan on telling my surgeons about your products. Hopefully, they will tell other patients’ there is a different route' to take. Thank You”</p>",
            "author": "Janice H.",
            "show_verified": true
          }
        },
        "review_mW8Riq": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "rating": 5,
            "headline": "Thank you for helping me look normal again!",
            "text": "<p>“I have a box full of breast forms and each one looked terrible. The shape was wrong, the size was wrong and I was discouraged. I thought I'd give Honey Cloudz a try and I'm so glad I did.<strong> It's as close to my existing breast as I can get. I don't look lopsided anymore and it doesn't shift. </strong>I don't have to constantly adjust. Thank you for helping me look normal again!”</p>",
            "author": "Barbara",
            "show_verified": true
          }
        },
        "review_GpFEAn": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "rating": 5,
            "headline": "This has helped to balance things out",
            "text": "<p>“I recently had a lumpectomy and am slightly smaller on one side now. This has helped to balance things out. <strong>It is very comfortable and doesn't move around.</strong> Very happy I found this product.”</p>",
            "author": "Serena V.",
            "show_verified": true
          }
        },
        "review_47HJzh": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "rating": 5,
            "headline": "I thought I had nothing to lose, and it turned out I have everything to gain!",
            "text": "<p>“Five years ago this month I had my mastectomy I had a radical one sided mastectomy. For five years, I have felt lopsided and not myself. I had what my insurance provided for a prosthetic insert and have worn it for five years. After wearing it for five years, I found that it was very heavy and lopsided. Having worn it for so long I started having shoulder pain with a knot and was told that it was from the heaviness of my prothesis insert. My Dr actually recommended for me to go without. I am sure all women out there understand that was not going to happen. So I started researching and found, honey cloudz! I thought I had nothing to lose, and it turned out I have everything to gain! <strong>Not only did it make me feel whole again, but it is so lightweight that it took care of the knot that was forming on my shoulder</strong>. If you were on the fence on going with this brand for a mastectomy, please go ahead and buy it. You won't regret it.\"</p>",
            "author": "Lisa R.",
            "show_verified": true
          }
        },
        "review_qhBVAG": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "rating": 5,
            "headline": "I feel so much better and happy my search is over",
            "text": "<p>“Having asymmetrical breasts I have always looked for solutions and never found anything great. I was careful not to get my hopes up too high with this form. It has surpassed every other solution<strong> I have tried. It fits easily into all my bras and swimsuits. I have went hiking, swimming and even wore them to a wedding. </strong>I feel so much better and happy my search is over. I am a full cup difference, a D cup and C cup”</p>",
            "author": "Vanessa L.",
            "show_verified": true
          }
        }
      },
